N5008 [expr.cast]/1, [dcl.ambig.res]: `(T)(x) - y' was verified as
`(T)(x - y)', `(f)(*p)' was rejected as `f * p', and `(p[1]) - 2' as a cast
to an array type.  The parser cannot tell whether a parenthesized name is a
type; the type checker now regroups the operators once it has looked the
name up.
